{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For there are many things</b>. Besides the soul's going after the desires of the world to gather wealth — such as seeking dominion and words of passion — all of them and their like multiply vapor; they add to a person's vapor. It is enough for him that he is vapor. This verse too turns upon the poor man who knows, that it is fitting for him to guard himself from all vapor, for what more does he have?"], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:57.969671512Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}